From 64ab5927ce832a6d59383d9632e27ae652495809 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ashish Kumar Singh <ashishkmr472@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 04:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] [XLA:GPU] Backport: output-to-operand aliasing in
 DynamicSliceFusionV2, and every operand use checked before sharing buffers

Two upstream commits, unchanged, on XLA d867969800:
- 63ed7d6a6f "[XLA:GPU] Support output-to-operand aliasing in DynamicSliceFusionV2" (PiperOrigin-RevId 1002127461).
- bdf1e5789f "Check all operand uses before sharing buffers" (openxla/xla#51490, Henning Becker).
A dynamic-slice fusion around a cuBLAS GEMM with beta 1 whose output, accumulator and a slice operand share one
buffer (B == C == D) read its operand after the GEMM began writing it, a write-after-read race on an A100;
buffer sharing now checks every use of an operand, not its first.
